  "findings": [
    "All four captures prove a clean Apple M4 Pro Metal binary, the expected implementation and entrypoint, complete profile-region markers, and exact trailing warmup/profile dispatch counts with no command-buffer collisions or duplicate interval groups.",
    "Packed QKV reduces submitted projection dispatches by exactly three: hot 3 to 1 per iteration and ring24 72 to 24. The profiled sequences contain 300 versus 100 and 7200 versus 2400 measured dispatches, respectively.",
    "The packed dispatch has a longer median GPU interval because it computes all 1152 outputs, while a baseline dispatch computes only Q, K, or V. Complete-workload timing, not per-dispatch duration, remains the valid comparison.",
    "Instrumented profile windows and target GPU-busy time moved in the same direction as ordinary timing, but profiler overhead prevents substituting those values for benchmark latency.",
    "Candidate captures showed higher device-wide occupancy, inflight SIMD groups, read bandwidth, MMU limiter, and last-level-cache limiter medians. These are single captures with different performance-state histories; they show a wider active workload but do not establish why ordinary timing improved.",
    "No target compiler-spill event and zero sampled threadgroup-memory L1 read/write bandwidth appeared in any capture. These are capture-bounded observations, not universal absence claims."
  ],
  "decision": "The profiles validate the intended one-enqueue composition and support the preregistered timing promotion. They do not add a cache, bandwidth, occupancy, or scheduling mechanism claim."
